    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nON VIEW SATURDAY 03RD OCTOBER 10.30AM - 11AM.\n\nNo. 75 Hardiman Road is a simply stunning 3 bedroom family home that has been architecturally extended and renovated into a beautiful modern home while located on a mature and established road in Drumcondra. This family-friendly neighbourhood, benefits from a strong sense of community and is within close proximity to a range of excellent schools and local amenities. \nThe accommodation comprises of an entrance area with a home office space and under stairs storage. A spacious living room and steps down to the bright and airy kitchen / dining room. Upstairs are 3 bedrooms and main family bathroom.\n \nTo the front, the property offers off-street parking and a mature garden planted with a variety of flowers and shrubs. The south facing rear garden has been carefully designed to create a peaceful and relaxing area with mature shrubs and natural stone paving. A storage unit is located at the rear of the garden. \n\nThe location is simply superb within walking distance of the city centre and convenient to the numerous shops, cafes, bars and restaurants Drumcondra Village has to offer. Na Fianna GAA club, The Botanic Gardens, Griffith Park, and Albert College Park are great local amenities. Dublin City University, St. Patricks College, Marino Institute of Education, along with a host of popular primary and secondary schools are within easy walking distance. Beaumont Hospital and the Mater Hospital are all within easy reach. Commuting further afield is made very easy with the M50 Motorway, The M1 and Dublin Airport within a few minutes' drive. The area is very well serviced by public transport, through the many bus routes which pass close by and Drumcondra Rail station nearby."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance area: - \nwith polished concrete floors, access to a large under stair storage closet and home office area.\n\nLiving Area - 4.34mx 6.30m\nwith polished concrete flooring, open fire with restored cast iron and emerald green tiles surround.\n\nKitchen & Dining room: - 3.78m x 4.77m\nwith polished concrete floors ample storage units with natural Quartzite stone worktop and splashback. A large full height sliding door gives access to the rear garden.\n\nBedroom One - 2.54m x 4.00m\ndouble room with wooden flooring and built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom Two - 2.55m x 2.34m\ndouble room with wooden flooring located to the front of the house.\n\nBedroom Three - 1.80m x 2.34m\nlocated to the front of the house with wooden flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.70m x 2.22m\nwith bath, shower whb and wc,\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>B energy rating</li><li>Under floor heating throughout the ground floor</li><li>Gas heating </li><li>Fully renovated </li><li>Extended to the rear</li><li>Positioned close to Griffith Park</li><li>Contemporary design</ul>"
      },
